IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `coa-core`
IMPORT `coa4-general-duties`
IMPORT `coa4-declaration`
IMPORT `coa4-approval-loans`
IMPORT `coa5-loans-exceptions`
IMPORT `coa-proc-director-interests`

-- coa-proc-director-interests-tests.l4: tests for coa-proc-director-interests.l4 (Companies Act 2006, ss 177, 182 to 184, 197, 204, 207, 213 and 214).
-- Every expected outcome is written from the text of the section named beside it, before the run, and never copied from the output.
-- A #TRACE prints FULFILLED, a BREACH or a still-open obligation (RESIDUAL) and no assertion line, so the expected outcome sits on the
-- `-- EXPECT` line directly above each trace and is read against the Result block by expect_check.py.
-- Day 0 and the unit of AT differ by rule and are given in the TIMELINE line above each rule; in these traces day 0 is 1 March 2026.

§ `Tests for the director's interests and loans procedure`

§§ `Assertions: the helpers`

-- s 177(4): the company enters into the transaction on 11 March, so on 1 March it has not yet done so; on the same day it has.
#ASSERT `s 177(4) the company has not yet entered into the transaction on the day the duty to declare arises` (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 11 3 2026)
#ASSERT (NOT (`s 177(4) the company has not yet entered into the transaction on the day the duty to declare arises` (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 1 3 2026)))
-- s 177(4): "before the company enters into": entry on day 10 (11 March) leaves day 10, the day of entry, as the last day for the declaration (a declaration that day, before entry, is in time).
#ASSERT (`s 177(4) the last day for the declaration, counted from day 0` (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 11 3 2026)) EQUALS 10
-- s 182(4): the caller's last day, 15 March, is 14 days after day 0; a last day before day 0 is read as day 0.
#ASSERT (`s 182(4) the days allowed, counted from day 0` (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 15 3 2026)) EQUALS 14
#ASSERT (`s 182(4) the days allowed, counted from day 0` (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 28 2 2026)) EQUALS 0
-- s 214: a last day of 31 March is 30 days after day 0.
#ASSERT (`s 214 the days in a reasonable period, counted from day 0` (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 31 3 2026)) EQUALS 30
-- s 204(1) and (2): funds for the company's purposes, 40,000 and 10,000 pounds in aggregate (50,000 does not exceed 50,000): the exception applies.
#ASSERT `s 204 the exception for expenditure on company business disapplies the requirement of approval` TRUE FALSE FALSE 40000 10000
-- s 204(2): 50,001 pounds exceeds the limit, so the section does not authorise the transaction.
#ASSERT (NOT (`s 204 the exception for expenditure on company business disapplies the requirement of approval` TRUE FALSE FALSE 40000 10001))
-- s 204(1): the thing done is not expenditure on company business.
#ASSERT (NOT (`s 204 the exception for expenditure on company business disapplies the requirement of approval` FALSE FALSE FALSE 100 0))
-- s 207(1): a loan of exactly 10,000 pounds and no other relevant transaction: the aggregate does not exceed 10,000 pounds.
#ASSERT `s 207(1) the exception for a small loan disapplies the requirement of approval` `s 207 a loan` (`s 211 a specific sum` 10_000) (`s 211 a specific sum` 0)
-- s 207(1): 10,001 pounds exceeds the sum.
#ASSERT (NOT (`s 207(1) the exception for a small loan disapplies the requirement of approval` `s 207 a loan` (`s 211 a specific sum` 10_001) (`s 211 a specific sum` 0)))
-- s 207(1) speaks of a loan or quasi-loan, not a credit transaction (that is s 207(2)).
#ASSERT (NOT (`s 207(1) the exception for a small loan disapplies the requirement of approval` `s 207 a credit transaction` (`s 211 a specific sum` 5_000) (`s 211 a specific sum` 0)))
-- s 197(3)(b)(i): the memorandum at the registered office for not less than 15 days ending with the meeting day: first day 1 March, meeting 15 March is 15 days.
#ASSERT (`s 197(3) the memorandum has been made available to members as the subsection requires` `at a meeting on a show of hands` TRUE FALSE (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 15 3 2026) TRUE) EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- s 197(3)(b)(i): meeting on 14 March is 14 days, one short.
#ASSERT (`s 197(3) the memorandum has been made available to members as the subsection requires` `at a meeting on a show of hands` TRUE FALSE (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 14 3 2026) TRUE) EQUALS JUST FALSE

§§ `Traces: s 177(1) and (4), the director declares before the company enters into the transaction (entry 11 March, last day for the declaration day 10, the day of entry)`

-- s 177(4): the director declares on day 3, before entry.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 177(1) and (4) the director's duty to declare before the company enters into the transaction` TRUE (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 11 3 2026) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 177-214 the director` DOES `s 177(1) the director declares the nature and extent of the interest to the other directors` AT 3

-- s 177(4): the declaration on day 9, the day before the day of entry.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 177(1) and (4) the director's duty to declare before the company enters into the transaction` TRUE (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 11 3 2026) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 177-214 the director` DOES `s 177(1) the director declares the nature and extent of the interest to the other directors` AT 9

-- s 177(4): the declaration on day 10, the day the company enters into the transaction, is in time: a declaration before entry that day complies.
-- EXPECT changed after independent review: a declaration on the day of entry, before the company enters into the transaction that day, is made before entry and complies with s 177(4) (src:2372)
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 177(1) and (4) the director's duty to declare before the company enters into the transaction` TRUE (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 11 3 2026) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 177-214 the director` DOES `s 177(1) the director declares the nature and extent of the interest to the other directors` AT 10

-- s 177(4): the declaration on day 11, the day after the company enters into the transaction, is not before it.
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `s 177(1) and (4) the director's duty to declare before the company enters into the transaction` TRUE (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 11 3 2026) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 177-214 the director` DOES `s 177(1) the director declares the nature and extent of the interest to the other directors` AT 11

-- s 177(1): the director never declares.
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `s 177(1) and (4) the director's duty to declare before the company enters into the transaction` TRUE (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 11 3 2026) AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 20)

-- s 177(5): the director is not aware of the interest, so the section requires no declaration and the rule has no duty.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 177(1) and (4) the director's duty to declare before the company enters into the transaction` TRUE (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 11 3 2026) AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 20)

-- s 177(6)(b): the other directors are already aware of the interest, so a declaration is not needed.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 177(1) and (4) the director's duty to declare before the company enters into the transaction` TRUE (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 11 3 2026) AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 20)

-- s 177(1): the company entered into the transaction on day 0, so it is not a proposed transaction and s 177 gives no duty (s 182 governs).
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 177(1) and (4) the director's duty to declare before the company enters into the transaction` TRUE (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 1 3 2026) AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 20)

§§ `Traces: s 177(3) and (4), a further declaration before the company enters into the transaction`

-- s 177(3) and (4): the declaration becomes inaccurate on day 0, and the further declaration is made on day 9, the day before the day of entry.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 177(3) and (4) the director's duty to make a further declaration before the company enters into the transaction` TRUE (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 11 3 2026) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 177-214 the director` DOES `s 177(3) the director makes a further declaration to the other directors` AT 9

-- s 177(3) and (4): the further declaration on day 10, the day of entry, is in time.
-- EXPECT changed after independent review: a further declaration on the day of entry, before the company enters into the transaction that day, is made before entry and complies with s 177(4) (src:2372)
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 177(3) and (4) the director's duty to make a further declaration before the company enters into the transaction` TRUE (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 11 3 2026) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 177-214 the director` DOES `s 177(3) the director makes a further declaration to the other directors` AT 10

-- s 177(3) and (4): the further declaration on day 11, the day after the day of entry, is too late.
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `s 177(3) and (4) the director's duty to make a further declaration before the company enters into the transaction` TRUE (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 11 3 2026) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 177-214 the director` DOES `s 177(3) the director makes a further declaration to the other directors` AT 11

-- s 177(3): the declaration has not become inaccurate or incomplete, so no further declaration is required.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 177(3) and (4) the director's duty to make a further declaration before the company enters into the transaction` FALSE (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 11 3 2026) AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 20)

§§ `Traces: s 182(1), (2) and (4) and s 183(1), the declaration as soon as is reasonably practicable (last day 15 March, day 14)`

-- s 182(2)(a) and (4): the director declares at a meeting on day 5, in time.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 182(4) and s 183(1) the director's duty to declare as soon as is reasonably practicable` TRUE FALSE (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 15 3 2026) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 177-214 the director` DOES `s 182(2)(a) the director declares at a meeting of the directors` AT 5

-- s 182(2)(b) and (4): the director declares by notice in writing on day 14, the last day.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 182(4) and s 183(1) the director's duty to declare as soon as is reasonably practicable` TRUE FALSE (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 15 3 2026) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 177-214 the director` DOES `s 182(2)(b) the director declares by notice in writing` AT 14

-- s 182(2)(c) and (4): the director declares by general notice on day 15, one day after the last day; s 183(1) makes the failure an offence.
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `s 182(4) and s 183(1) the director's duty to declare as soon as is reasonably practicable` TRUE FALSE (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 15 3 2026) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 177-214 the director` DOES `s 182(2)(c) the director declares by general notice` AT 15

-- s 182(4) and s 183(1): the director never declares.
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `s 182(4) and s 183(1) the director's duty to declare as soon as is reasonably practicable` TRUE FALSE (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 15 3 2026) AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 30)

-- s 182(1), second sentence: the interest has been declared under s 177, so s 182 does not apply.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 182(4) and s 183(1) the director's duty to declare as soon as is reasonably practicable` TRUE TRUE (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 15 3 2026) AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 30)

§§ `Traces: s 182(1), the underlying duty that a late declaration still discharges (s 182(4), second sentence)`

-- s 182(4): "failure to comply with this requirement does not affect the underlying duty": a declaration at a meeting on day 40, long after any reasonable time, still discharges it.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 182(1) the director's underlying duty to declare, which a late declaration still discharges` TRUE FALSE (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 177-214 the director` DOES `s 182(2)(a) the director declares at a meeting of the directors` AT 40

-- s 182(1): no declaration by day 40; the duty is still owed and no clock ends it.
-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `s 182(1) the director's underlying duty to declare, which a late declaration still discharges` TRUE FALSE (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 40)

-- s 182(1), second sentence: the interest has been declared under s 177, so s 182 does not apply and the director owes nothing under it.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 182(1) the director's underlying duty to declare, which a late declaration still discharges` TRUE TRUE (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 40)

§§ `Traces: s 197(1) and (2), the company's loan to a director`

-- s 197(1)(a): the company makes a loan to a director without a resolution of the members and no exception applies.
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `s 197(1) the company's duty not to make or secure a loan to a director without the members' approval` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE NOTHING FALSE (JUST FALSE) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 177-214 the company` DOES `s 197(1) the company makes the loan or gives the guarantee or provides the security` AT 4

-- s 197(1): the company has not made the loan; the prohibition stays open, with no clock.
-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `s 197(1) the company's duty not to make or secure a loan to a director without the members' approval` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE NOTHING FALSE (JUST FALSE) AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 30)

-- s 197(1)(b): the company gives a guarantee in connection with a loan by another person to a director, without approval.
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `s 197(1) the company's duty not to make or secure a loan to a director without the members' approval` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE NOTHING FALSE (JUST FALSE) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 177-214 the company` DOES `s 197(1) the company makes the loan or gives the guarantee or provides the security` AT 4

-- s 197(1): "unless the transaction has been approved by a resolution of the members": approved, so the company may make the loan.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 197(1) the company's duty not to make or secure a loan to a director without the members' approval` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE NOTHING FALSE (JUST FALSE) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 177-214 the company` DOES `s 197(1) the company makes the loan or gives the guarantee or provides the security` AT 4

-- s 204: the funds are for the company's purposes, 30,000 pounds and 10,000 pounds in aggregate, so approval is not required.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 197(1) the company's duty not to make or secure a loan to a director without the members' approval` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE NOTHING (`s 204 the exception for expenditure on company business disapplies the requirement of approval` TRUE FALSE FALSE 30000 10000) (JUST FALSE) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 177-214 the company` DOES `s 197(1) the company makes the loan or gives the guarantee or provides the security` AT 4

-- s 207(1): a loan of 10,000 pounds alone does not exceed the sum, so approval is not required.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 197(1) the company's duty not to make or secure a loan to a director without the members' approval` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE NOTHING (`s 207(1) the exception for a small loan disapplies the requirement of approval` `s 207 a loan` (`s 211 a specific sum` 10_000) (`s 211 a specific sum` 0)) (JUST FALSE) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 177-214 the company` DOES `s 197(1) the company makes the loan or gives the guarantee or provides the security` AT 4

-- s 207(1): a loan of 10,001 pounds exceeds the sum, so the exception is lost and the loan without approval is a breach.
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `s 197(1) the company's duty not to make or secure a loan to a director without the members' approval` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE NOTHING (`s 207(1) the exception for a small loan disapplies the requirement of approval` `s 207 a loan` (`s 211 a specific sum` 10_001) (`s 211 a specific sum` 0)) (JUST FALSE) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 177-214 the company` DOES `s 197(1) the company makes the loan or gives the guarantee or provides the security` AT 4

-- s 197(2): the members of the company approved, but the director is a director of the holding company and its members have not (the answer under s 197(2) is JUST TRUE).
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `s 197(1) the company's duty not to make or secure a loan to a director without the members' approval` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE NOTHING FALSE (JUST TRUE) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 177-214 the company` DOES `s 197(1) the company makes the loan or gives the guarantee or provides the security` AT 4

-- s 197(1): the borrower is not a director of the company or of its holding company, so s 197 does not bar the loan.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 197(1) the company's duty not to make or secure a loan to a director without the members' approval` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE NOTHING FALSE (JUST FALSE) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 177-214 the company` DOES `s 197(1) the company makes the loan or gives the guarantee or provides the security` AT 4

§§ `Traces: s 197(3) and (4), the memorandum before the resolution (meeting 15 March is 15 days from 1 March; 14 March is 14 days)`

-- s 197(3)(b)(i): the memorandum has been at the registered office for 15 days ending with the meeting day and is at the meeting; the members pass the resolution.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 197(3) the members' duty not to pass the resolution without the memorandum made available` `at a meeting on a show of hands` TRUE FALSE (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 15 3 2026) TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 177-214 the members of the company` DOES `s 197(3) the members pass the resolution approving the transaction` AT 0

-- s 197(3)(b)(i): the memorandum has been at the registered office for only 14 days ending with the meeting day; passing the resolution is a breach.
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `s 197(3) the members' duty not to pass the resolution without the memorandum made available` `at a meeting on a show of hands` TRUE FALSE (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 14 3 2026) TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 177-214 the members of the company` DOES `s 197(3) the members pass the resolution approving the transaction` AT 0

-- s 197(3)(b)(i): 16 days is "not less than 15 days"; the members pass the resolution.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 197(3) the members' duty not to pass the resolution without the memorandum made available` `at a meeting on a show of hands` TRUE FALSE (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 16 3 2026) TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 177-214 the members of the company` DOES `s 197(3) the members pass the resolution approving the transaction` AT 0

-- s 197(3)(b)(ii): the memorandum was not available at the meeting itself, so passing the resolution is a breach.
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `s 197(3) the members' duty not to pass the resolution without the memorandum made available` `at a meeting on a show of hands` TRUE FALSE (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 15 3 2026) FALSE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 177-214 the members of the company` DOES `s 197(3) the members pass the resolution approving the transaction` AT 0

-- s 197(3) and (4): the memorandum does not set out the matters in subsection (4); passing the resolution is a breach.
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `s 197(3) the members' duty not to pass the resolution without the memorandum made available` `at a meeting on a show of hands` FALSE FALSE (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 15 3 2026) TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 177-214 the members of the company` DOES `s 197(3) the members pass the resolution approving the transaction` AT 0

-- s 197(3)(a): a written resolution; the memorandum was sent to every eligible member at or before the time the proposed resolution was sent; the members pass it.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 197(3) the members' duty not to pass the resolution without the memorandum made available` `as a written resolution` TRUE TRUE (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 15 3 2026) FALSE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 177-214 the members of the company` DOES `s 197(3) the members pass the resolution approving the transaction` AT 0

-- s 197(3)(a): a written resolution; the memorandum was not sent to every eligible member in time; passing it is a breach.
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `s 197(3) the members' duty not to pass the resolution without the memorandum made available` `as a written resolution` TRUE FALSE (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 15 3 2026) FALSE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 177-214 the members of the company` DOES `s 197(3) the members pass the resolution approving the transaction` AT 0

-- s 197(3): the memorandum falls short (14 days) and the members have not passed the resolution; the prohibition stays open.
-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `s 197(3) the members' duty not to pass the resolution without the memorandum made available` `at a meeting on a show of hands` TRUE FALSE (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 14 3 2026) TRUE AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 30)

§§ `Traces: s 213(2), the company's power to avoid a transaction made in contravention`

-- s 213(2): the section applies and none of (a), (b) or (c) holds; the company avoids the transaction on day 40 (no time limit is stated).
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 213(2) the company's power to avoid the transaction or arrangement` (JUST TRUE) FALSE FALSE FALSE (JUST FALSE) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 177-214 the company` DOES `s 213(2) the company avoids the transaction or arrangement` AT 40

-- s 213(2): the company has not avoided it; the power stays open, with no clock.
-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `s 213(2) the company's power to avoid the transaction or arrangement` (JUST TRUE) FALSE FALSE FALSE (JUST FALSE) AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 100)

-- s 213(2)(a): restitution is no longer possible, so the transaction is not voidable and the company has no power to avoid it.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 213(2) the company's power to avoid the transaction or arrangement` (JUST TRUE) TRUE FALSE FALSE (JUST FALSE) AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 100)

-- s 213(2)(b): the company has been indemnified for the loss, so the transaction is not voidable and the company has no power to avoid it.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 213(2) the company's power to avoid the transaction or arrangement` (JUST TRUE) FALSE TRUE FALSE (JUST FALSE) AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 100)

-- s 213(2)(c): rights acquired in good faith, for value and without notice, by a person who is not a party would be affected, so no power to avoid.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 213(2) the company's power to avoid the transaction or arrangement` (JUST TRUE) FALSE FALSE TRUE (JUST FALSE) AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 100)

-- s 214: the transaction was affirmed by resolution within a reasonable period, so it "may no longer be avoided under section 213".
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 213(2) the company's power to avoid the transaction or arrangement` (JUST TRUE) FALSE FALSE FALSE (JUST TRUE) AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 100)

§§ `Traces: s 213(3) to (7), the persons liable account for the gain and indemnify the company`

-- s 213(3)(a) and (b): a person liable under (4) made a gain and the company suffered loss; the person accounts on day 10 and indemnifies on day 20.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 213(3) the duty of each person liable to account for the gain and indemnify the company` (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) TRUE TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 177-214 a person liable under section 213(4)` DOES `s 213(3)(a) the person accounts to the company for the gain` AT 10
    PARTY `ss 177-214 a person liable under section 213(4)` DOES `s 213(3)(b) the person indemnifies the company for the loss or damage` AT 20

-- s 213(3): only the account is made; the indemnity is still owed, with no clock.
-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `s 213(3) the duty of each person liable to account for the gain and indemnify the company` (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) TRUE TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 177-214 a person liable under section 213(4)` DOES `s 213(3)(a) the person accounts to the company for the gain` AT 10

-- s 213(6): the director shows he took all reasonable steps, so is not liable by virtue of (4)(c).
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 213(3) the duty of each person liable to account for the gain and indemnify the company` (JUST TRUE) (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) TRUE TRUE AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 50)

-- s 213(3)(a): there is no gain, and the company has suffered loss; only the indemnity is owed and it is given on day 5.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 213(3) the duty of each person liable to account for the gain and indemnify the company` (JUST TRUE) (JUST FALSE) (JUST FALSE) FALSE TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 177-214 a person liable under section 213(4)` DOES `s 213(3)(b) the person indemnifies the company for the loss or damage` AT 5

§§ `Traces: s 214, the members affirm within a reasonable period (day 0 is 1 March 2026; last day 31 March, day 30)`

-- s 214: the members affirm by resolution on day 10, within a reasonable period.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 214 the members' power to affirm the transaction or arrangement` (JUST TRUE) (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 31 3 2026) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 177-214 the members of the company` DOES `s 214 the members of the company affirm the transaction or arrangement by resolution` AT 10

-- s 214: the members affirm on day 30, the last day of the reasonable period.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 214 the members' power to affirm the transaction or arrangement` (JUST TRUE) (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 31 3 2026) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 177-214 the members of the company` DOES `s 214 the members of the company affirm the transaction or arrangement by resolution` AT 30

-- s 214: no affirmation by day 10; the reasonable period (to day 30) is still running, so the power to affirm is still open.
-- EXPECT RESIDUAL
#TRACE `s 214 the members' power to affirm the transaction or arrangement` (JUST TRUE) (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 31 3 2026) AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 10)

-- s 214: no affirmation by day 31; the period has lapsed and nothing follows from the lapse (the company's power to avoid is the rule above and stays open).
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 214 the members' power to affirm the transaction or arrangement` (JUST TRUE) (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 31 3 2026) AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 31)

-- s 214: the members affirm on day 31, one day after the last day of the reasonable period; the affirmation is late and the rule has no step left to take (a late event after a lapsed MAY).
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 214 the members' power to affirm the transaction or arrangement` (JUST TRUE) (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 31 3 2026) AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `ss 177-214 the members of the company` DOES `s 214 the members of the company affirm the transaction or arrangement by resolution` AT 31

-- s 214 applies only where the transaction was entered into in contravention (s 213(1) is JUST FALSE here), so there is no power to affirm and nothing is open at day 10.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `s 214 the members' power to affirm the transaction or arrangement` (JUST FALSE) (Date 1 3 2026) (Date 31 3 2026) AT 0 WITH
    (WAITUNTIL 10)

-- READS-DIFFERENTLY-ON-MAIN:
-- No trace in this file differs in class (FULFILLED, BREACH, RESIDUAL) between the unstable build (a50cbd0, 25 November 2026) and main (112):
-- all 53 traces match their EXPECT on both. The Result block prints differently on main in four traces, all with the same class on both:
--   * the two traces of `s 182(4) and s 183(1)` that breach (a declaration by general notice on day 15; no declaration by day 30): the ROR has three
--     alternatives and all three breach; unstable joins the breaches with BY under one BREACH, main joins them with OR DEONTIC BREACHED.
--   * the two traces with an open prohibition (`s 197(1)` with no loan made; `s 197(3)` with no resolution passed): unstable prints the LEST with its
--     BREACH in parentheses, main without.
-- The lapsed MAY of `s 214` (LEST FULFILLED, waited to day 31) is FULFILLED on both.
